  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p19-q7-intro",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In this question we give a clever method for easily generating Pythagorean triples.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-q7-method",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "start": 1,
          "indent": 7,
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "p19-q7-method-1",
              "type": "list-item",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p19-q7-method-1-text",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "fontSize": null,
                  "align": "left",
                  "spaceBefore": 0,
                  "spaceAfter": 1,
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "indent": 0,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Pick any two odd numbers that differ by two, such as 3 and 5.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p19-q7-method-2",
              "type": "list-item",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p19-q7-method-2-text",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "fontSize": null,
                  "align": "left",
                  "spaceBefore": 0,
                  "spaceAfter": 1,
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "indent": 0,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Add their reciprocals. Here, ",
                      "marks": []
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "\\frac13+\\frac15=\\frac8{15}",
                      "display": false
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ".",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p19-q7-method-3",
              "type": "list-item",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p19-q7-method-3-text",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "fontSize": null,
                  "align": "left",
                  "spaceBefore": 0,
                  "spaceAfter": 1,
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "indent": 0,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The numerator and the denominator of the resulting fraction will be the first two terms of a Pythagorean triple. Here, the triple is ",
                      "marks": []
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "(8,15,17)",
                      "display": false
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", since ",
                      "marks": []
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "math",
                      "latex": "8^2+15^2=17^2",
                      "display": false
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ".",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q7-a",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the triple obtained if you begin with the numbers:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 3,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p19-q7-a-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "1 and 3",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$(3,4,5)$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac11+\\frac13&=\\frac43\\\\4^2+3^2&=16+9\\\\4^2+3^2&=25\\\\4^2+3^2&=5^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe triple is $(3,4,5)$, with the legs written in increasing order.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 60
          },
          {
            "id": "p19-q7-a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "3 and 5",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$(8,15,17)$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac13+\\frac15&=\\frac8{15}\\\\8^2+15^2&=64+225\\\\8^2+15^2&=289\\\\8^2+15^2&=17^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe triple is $(8,15,17)$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 52
          },
          {
            "id": "p19-q7-a-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "7 and 9",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$(16,63,65)$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac17+\\frac19&=\\frac{16}{63}\\\\16^2+63^2&=256+3969\\\\16^2+63^2&=4225\\\\16^2+63^2&=65^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe triple is $(16,63,65)$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 52
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Prove that this method always results in a Pythagorean triple.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For the positive odd numbers $2n-1$ and $2n+1$, the sum is $\\frac{4n}{4n^2-1}$ and the triple is $(4n,4n^2-1,4n^2+1)$, with $n\\geq1$.\n\nExpanding shows $(4n)^2+(4n^2-1)^2=(4n^2+1)^2$.",
          "worked": "Write the positive odd numbers as $2n-1$ and $2n+1$, where $n\\geq1$ is an integer.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{2n-1}+\\frac1{2n+1}&=\\frac{(2n+1)+(2n-1)}{(2n-1)(2n+1)}\\\\\\frac1{2n-1}+\\frac1{2n+1}&=\\frac{4n}{4n^2-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe numerator and denominator are positive integers. Also,\n$$\\begin{align*}(4n)^2+(4n^2-1)^2&=16n^2+16n^4-8n^2+1\\\\(4n)^2+(4n^2-1)^2&=16n^4+8n^2+1\\\\(4n)^2+(4n^2-1)^2&=(4n^2+1)^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(4n,4n^2-1,4n^2+1)$ is always a Pythagorean triple.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
